From 1f7eadaaa44ced8bb41cd8280532b88819e3fe32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:17:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Disable Square action execution honestly; add real Stripe
 billing at $30/$65

Square: OAuth connect still works, but buildImpactPlan now excludes Square
from every action plan regardless of connection status, so a voice command
that would have silently gone to Square instead surfaces the existing
'No configured delivery channel can execute this action yet.' message.
executor.ts also throws a clear error if a Square job ever reaches it, as a
defense-in-depth backstop. IntegrationsScreen now says so on the connected
card too.

Billing: Basic ($30/mo) and Enterprise ($65/mo) now go through real Stripe
Checkout (api/billing/checkout.ts) instead of the previous 'owner_test'
button that flipped the plan for free. A new webhook
(api/billing/webhook.ts) verifies Stripe's signature and activates/updates/
cancels the subscription from checkout.session.completed and
customer.subscription.updated/deleted. api/billing/switch.ts is now
free-plan-only, so there is no way to grant paid entitlements without an
actual Stripe payment, and downgrading to free cancels any active Stripe
subscription. BillingScreen and the MoreScreen billing modal open Stripe
Checkout in the browser and refresh the plan automatically when the app
regains focus. Corrected the placeholder $14.99/$29.99 prices everywhere,
including a new migration for the plans table.
